  "review": {
    "label": "curated_editorial",
    "look_ahead": "Glass would be dismissed in February 2022 after a bottom-six season, and the club would move through Robson and Goodwin before the next stable spell.\n",
    "read": "This is the hinge season. The results still look like the McInnes era, but the appointment of Stephen Glass changed the intended direction. Judging the new direction from the final league position alone would miss the point; the next season is where the cost of the transition becomes visible.\n",
    "trade_off": "Changing manager while holding a top-four finish protected the league floor but delayed the rebuild until the following season. The new manager inherited a squad shaped by the previous regime.\n",
    "what_did_not": "The League Cup exit came in the second round and the Scottish Cup run ended with a 3-0 defeat at Dundee United. The European campaign again stopped at the third qualifying round.\n",
    "what_worked": "The league position held at fourth and the club reached the Scottish Cup quarter-final. The managerial transition was orderly: one interim match, then a permanent appointment.\n"
  },
